    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><dateline><date when="1948-09-20">September 20, 1948</date></dateline>
                    <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Professor
                            Tillich</rs>:</salute></opener>
                <p>Some months ago I came across a notation to the effect that a book entitled <hi
                        rend="u">English</hi>
                    <hi rend="u">Writings</hi>
                    <hi rend="u">of</hi>
                    <hi rend="u">Dr</hi>. <hi rend="u">Tillich</hi> by <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__3883" type="person">Dillenberger</rs> was to be
                        published.<note type="ea">Vgl. <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3883"
                            type="person">John Dillenberger</rs>: <rs type="work"
                            ref="#tillich__AAUZJFJ3">English Writings of Dr. Tillich</rs>
                        (1947).</note> I have not been able to find additional information
                    concerning this, and I am writing you to learn if you can supply me with the
                    name of the publisher. I am enclosing a self-addressed envelope for your
                    convenience in answering this.</p>
                <p>I am</p>
                <closer><salute>Very truly yours,</salute><signed><hi rend="hand"><rs
                                ref="#tillich_person_id__5331" type="person">Raymond P.
                            Morris.</rs></hi><lb/><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__5331" type="person"
                            >Raymond P. Morris.</rs>, Librarian</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>RPM:js</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
